Kodak licensee Reto this week <a href="https://www.kodak.retopro.co/products/kodak-slidetag-br-keychain-photo-display-and-tracker-blind-box">introduced</a> the SlideTag, a &#36;34.99 Find My-compatible item tracker with a color E Ink screen for displaying personal photos.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/kodak-slidetag.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1079641" /><br/>
The SlideTag's design draws on Kodak's Kodachrome slide mounts, placing a square display inside a retro frame with an attachment point for a keyring. Its 1.54-inch screen has a resolution of 240 × 240 pixels and uses six ink colors to reproduce images. As it is an E Ink panel, it retains a static image without needing continuous power to display it.<br/>
<br/>
Users can manage photos through the Kodak Memory Link app for iOS and Android, separately from the accessory's tracking features. They can transfer up to 12 images over Bluetooth and arrange them into slideshows, or use the screen to display information such as contact details, a QR code, or a to-do list.<br/>
<br/>
Once paired with Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/find-my/">Find My</a> app, the SlideTag can be located through the &zwnj;Find My&zwnj; network. There is also support for Google's Find Hub. A built-in buzzer provides an audible way to find nearby belongings.<br/>
<br/>
The device uses a replaceable CR2032 battery and has an IP54 rating for dust and splash resistance. Its plastic enclosure measures 39.3 × 46 × 7.58mm and weighs 16.6 grams, making it wider and taller than the current <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airtag/">AirTag</a>, but slightly thinner. Apple's tracker measures 31.9mm in diameter and 8mm thick, and weighs 11.8 grams.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; retains some advantages, including Ultra Wideband technology for Precision Finding, which provides distance and directional guidance to nearby items on compatible devices. The &zwnj;AirTag&zwnj; also has a higher IP67 rating, providing protection against immersion in water up to one meter deep for up to 30 minutes.<br/>
<br/>
Reto, which also makes the Kodak-branded Charmera keychain camera, is selling the SlideTag as a collectible. Buyers receive a randomly selected design in sealed packaging, rather than choosing a particular finish. There are eight standard designs and a secret edition that has a one-in-64 chance of appearing.<br/>
<br/>
